# Security headers for the Bramble website.
#
# Cloudflare Workers parses this file out of the deployed asset directory and
# applies it to static-asset responses. It is not itself served as an asset.
# Vite copies public/ into dist/, so it ships with every build.
#
# Deliberately NOT set here:
#   Strict-Transport-Security and X-Content-Type-Options are configured at the
#   Cloudflare edge (SSL/TLS -> Edge Certificates). Setting them here as well
#   would emit them from two sources of truth; the edge is the one in use.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is enforcing. It shipped report-only first and was
# promoted only after its violations were read from a browser console on every
# page, because a wrong script-src or style-src does not degrade a single-page
# app, it blanks it. What was observed before promoting: React mounted, one
# stylesheet applied, both fonts loaded, eight images with none broken, the
# support form present, and no violations on /, /docs/, /support/ or /privacy/.
#
# The policy was derived from the built output, not assumed: scripts, styles,
# fonts and images are all same-origin under /assets or /, the external hosts in
# the bundle (Chrome Web Store, GitHub, Starkscan) are link targets rather than
# fetches and so need no fetch-directive allowance, and `data:` is allowed for
# images only because Vite inlines assets below its size threshold.
#
# form-action is 'self' rather than 'none'. The support page has a real <form>
# with no action attribute: its onSubmit calls preventDefault() and navigates,
# but without JavaScript the form would submit to the current document, and
# 'none' would block that path.
#
# Anything added to this site that loads from a new origin — an analytics
# script, an embedded video, a webfont from a CDN — will now be BLOCKED rather
# than reported. Add the origin to the matching directive in the same change,
# and re-verify in a browser.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'; manifest-src 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), bluetooth=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), hid=(), idle-detection=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), screen-wake-lock=(), serial=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
